This project demonstrates a two-tier web application using Flask as the application layer and MySQL as the database layer, fully containerized using Docker and orchestrated with Docker Compose.
The application is deployed and managed via Jenkins CI/CD.

User
 │
 │ HTTP (Port 5000)
 ▼
Flask Application (Container)
 │
 │ Internal Docker Network
 ▼
MySQL Database (Container)


Components

Flask App: Handles HTTP requests, business logic, and DB interactions

MySQL: Stores application data

Docker Compose: Manages multi-container setup

Jenkins: Automates build and deployment


🚀 Application Functionality

Displays a web page served by Flask

Accepts user input (messages)

Stores messages in a MySQL database

Fetches and displays the latest message

Includes health checks for container monitoring


🔁 CI/CD with Jenkins

The Jenkins pipeline performs:

Clones the GitHub repository

Stops existing containers

Builds Docker images using Docker Compose

Deploys the application

Verifies running containers